    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0346" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/3043: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-12T17:00:00-04:00">May 12, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Your 315, May 5. Department welcomes your promptness in beginning the
                    preliminary conversations. The Department’s only suggestion at this time is that
                    too great emphasis by you on the adviser question may create the impression that
                    our suggestion of general discussions was merely to accomplish the specific end
                    of support for the advisers. The Department hopes that during the discussions
                    the British or Russians, preferably the latter, will offer suggestions for
                    implementing the program of assistance to Iran, and that these suggestions will
                    include more equitable financial agreements with Iran and better facilities for
                    Iranian officials, including the American advisers, to operate throughout the
                    country.</p>
                <pb facs="0347" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/>
                <p>The purpose of the discussions is to bring about genuine and effective
                    American-Soviet-British cooperation in Iran. You should repeatedly emphasize
                    this desire on the part of the United States.</p>
                <p>Department is sending you by airmail copies of memoranda of conversations bearing
                    on Iran which took place in London between officers of the Department and
                    British officials.</p>
                <p>Please repeat your telegrams on this subject to Moscow and London.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tehran, repeated to London and Moscow.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d336-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
